This pipeline adopts the Orthofinder 3 new procedure, where "high quality" proteomes were used to estimate an initial set of orthogroups.
The phylogenetically hierarchical orthogroup at node N1 (corresponding to the teleost node after WGD) was picked to define orthogroups.
Then, other proteomes were assigned to these orthogroups with the "assign" feature of orthofinder 3.

Finally, species containing paralogs were masked in the ortholog table with NA.
